Build a binary that runs on every worker, not only on the one that built it.

The image is built on the swarm manager and the service can be scheduled on any
node. `-march=native -mtune=native` bakes in the manager's instruction set, so
the binary SIGILLs on a worker with an older CPU -- a crash that looks like a
method bug and is really a build flag.

`-Ofast` stays: it is what upstream asks for, and dropping only the two tuning
flags is the smallest change that makes the binary portable. (This replaces a
`sed` that rewrote both flags to `-O3`, leaving `-Ofast -O3`; -ffast-math
survives a later -O3, so that produced the same code generation as plain
-Ofast, just less legibly.)

Applies to SOURCE_REF=6fb9eccf7d9d6c1f49e6f28e71e6a79ab9e31b11.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 4d0ae7e..d1a507b 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ OBJS := $(SOURCES:.cpp=.o)
 
 .PHONY: clean
 
-optimized: CFLAGS += -Ofast -march=native -mtune=native
+optimized: CFLAGS += -Ofast
 optimized: streamspot
 
 debug: CFLAGS += -DDEBUG -g
